#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083065 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "27a80de6-49d0-557b-8444-ebab046e795b" :question/math-academy-id "e-6074" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a tetrahedral die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nA tetrahedral die has four sides. Let $X$ be the score attained on a random roll of the die. Then the support is $S = \\{ 1,2,3,4 \\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\dfrac{1}{4}{:}$\n\n$$\nf(1) = f(2) = f(3) = f(4) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083066 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90d0c882-c94b-5759-9a78-63979365e318" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Profit of a Game"}] :question/id #uuid "2b946455-893f-57db-b0a5-d52091914cf2" :question/math-academy-id "e-6075" :question/problem "Suppose that we play a game with a stack of five cards labeled $1$ through $5.$ A card is drawn at random. Drawing $1,2,3,$ or $4$ means that you lose $\\[math]1,$ and drawing a $5$ means that you win $\\[/math] 5.$ What is the expected profit at each drawing in this game?" :question/worked-solution "Let $p$ represent the profit on a draw in this game. On each draw in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- drawing $1,2,3,4$, the player loses $\\[math]1,$ so we have $p=-1.$\n\n- drawing $5$, the player wins $\\[/math]5,$ so we have $p=5.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(-1)=\\dfrac{4}{5}, \\qquad P(5)=\\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single draw, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $p$ | $-1$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(p)$ | $\\dfrac{4}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\textrm E[p] &= -1 \\cdot f(-1) + 5 \\cdot f(5)  \\[5pt]\n&= -1 \\left( \\dfrac{4}{5} \\right) + 5 \\left( \\dfrac{1}{5} \\right)  \\[5pt]\n\t&=-\\dfrac{4}{5} + 1 \\[3pt]\n\t&=\\dfrac{1}{5} \\[3pt]\n\t&=0.2\n\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit at each draw in this game is $\\[math]0.20$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083108 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "e6dd60de-5df1-531d-9971-847343303fd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-7383" :question/problem "The rolls of an unfair tetrahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{10})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{2}{5})+4(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{6}{5}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{12}{10}+\\frac{8}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+6+12+8}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{10} \\\\  & =2.7\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083109 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "ed80b546-956c-5b67-ac7d-0c0049c2278c" :question/math-academy-id "e-7385" :question/problem "Several children were asked about how many pets they have. The results were recorded below. If $X$ is the number of pets that a randomly selected child has, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of pets | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $5$ | $6$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of pets, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $5+6+5=16,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{5}{16} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{16}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{5}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{16}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{5}{16})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{5}{16}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{10}{16} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{6}{16}+\\frac{10}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+6+10}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{16} \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a55a640-5056-53aa-a01c-37549144e131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569544} {:answer/id #uuid "69532553-7c14-5c9e-8f67-52df69fbcb70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569607} {:answer/id #uuid "a4821310-860e-5fda-9174-3a8a5f122a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{53}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569707} {:answer/id #uuid "ba42e326-790d-5ce1-a2d5-97a6580a41b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569739} {:answer/id #uuid "ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba66511f-5970-5a6f-9b8a-e517905c7f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569741} :answer-field/id #uuid "57adae38-47d4-5119-8e1b-753ad3c2f4c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53e1317a-3ae2-58ac-bb4d-59a740997145" :question/math-academy-id "q-127259" :question/problem "The rolls of an unfair octahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{16})+3(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{32})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{32})+7(\\frac{1}{4})+8(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{2}{16}+\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{4}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{12}{32}+\\frac{20}{32}+\\frac{6}{32}+\\frac{56}{32}+\\frac{64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+6+12+20+6+56+64}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e77bbba-6d78-5114-b600-9c7f71e65420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260009} {:answer/id #uuid "447f8063-1baf-5c4a-9b97-4a25fc328415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260473} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec2e1ee-da93-5494-b50c-58b008ea1ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260545} {:answer/id #uuid "85075ebd-c155-585d-a463-64d1c425a07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261030} {:answer/id #uuid "b0beacca-b6b9-5b56-9e34-2ad8f29a0929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec2e1ee-da93-5494-b50c-58b008ea1ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260545} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd47829e-aabc-5fbe-b4ee-de0c0b559504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e811f3df-a27f-5fdf-9386-dd1c84fc9cd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127269" :question/problem "The absolute difference between the outcomes of one roll of two fair six-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the absolute difference of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{5}{18}$ | $\\frac{4}{18}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{2}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{5}{18})+2(\\frac{4}{18})+3(\\frac{3}{18})+4(\\frac{2}{18})+5(\\frac{1}{18}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{9}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+8+9+8+5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90d0c882-c94b-5759-9a78-63979365e318" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Profit of a Game"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bec36d6-dfb7-5749-9664-f7f73dc25b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\$10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569485} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9bbeaf-98e6-558c-81d6-d0813fc9f4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\$19$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569509} {:answer/id #uuid "59a5f4bc-a0cc-5d8a-b1c9-87ca178ebcf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\$7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569572} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4ee2a5-d371-5586-98ed-838864441766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\$9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569669} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\$8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1e0eb6a-bd70-5f35-a14d-f4f095208cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\$8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569722} :answer-field/id #uuid "53865da6-8e44-5bb9-8d40-4d2805caf8a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "068e9bc7-6f46-5ac9-a057-d5f4aa9a8aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-127818" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$1$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$35.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $12$ in a row?" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 1=100$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $35$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =35\\cdot f(35)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =35(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{38} \\\\  & ≈0.92.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games  on number $12$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (0.92)=92.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $100$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=92-100=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e15daab7-6b24-5c89-8928-f0f9fcd1b856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569803} :answer-field/id #uuid "36c5b657-8ae8-52f1-9b50-9850b824e02a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cdf7c4f-4409-57f0-b1eb-dca5de834f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-276297" :question/problem "A fair spinner has six sides labeled with the numbers $-2,$ $-1,$ $0,$ $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$ If the spinner is spun, what is the expected value of the outcome?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the outcome of the spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(0)=f(1)=f(2)=f(3)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =-2\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}+0+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+0+1+2+3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3a5e633-756d-5e3a-8fa9-0ed6225a69ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569705} :answer-field/id #uuid "55e2ebfb-2990-504c-a3b7-16d650b15125" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41c4d9f2-fb24-5742-893b-e72bc5478b30" :question/math-academy-id "q-276300" :question/problem "A quality control manager at a warehouse inspects electronic boxes for defective items. The number of faulty items in each box was recorded and summarized below. If $X$ is the number of faulty items in a box, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Boxes | $13$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Faulty Items | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the faulty items, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of boxes is $13+6+4+2=25,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{13}{25} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{25} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{4}{25} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{13}{25})+1(\\frac{6}{25})+2(\\frac{4}{25})+3(\\frac{2}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}+\\frac{8}{25}+\\frac{6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+8+6}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee3a7f8d-4e6d-583c-9448-f641c8a25567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569820} :answer-field/id #uuid "eff3eb79-2efb-59dd-8b16-b566385dd9e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f220269-fce2-5308-a544-a882143be2b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-337038" :question/problem "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $3$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $3$ coins? Do not round the answer.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{9})+1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{9})+3(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+2+9}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{189}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2b4ec13-aabf-55f7-9a84-533146afb111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{189}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569726} :answer-field/id #uuid "05e35378-f763-5683-b2ea-96d534b870bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc6b2040-54a4-56f7-9767-230b7779b10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337188" :question/problem "The sum of the outcomes of one roll of two unfair four-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the sum of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{40}$ | $\\frac{7}{40}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7)+8\\cdot f(8) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3}{40})+3(\\frac{7}{40})+4(\\frac{1}{5})+5(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+6(\\frac{3}{20})+7(\\frac{1}{10})+8(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{18}{20}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{40}+\\frac{21}{40}+\\frac{32}{40}+\\frac{50}{40}+\\frac{36}{40}+\\frac{28}{40}+\\frac{16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+32+50+36+28+16}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{189}{40} \\\\  & =4.725.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48698d2-8399-5591-8858-d21e6e33a4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e295c467-cba5-5269-8303-2482a80e3bd4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ceddea1b-a5cb-5c22-91ab-6571fb7ef388" :question/math-academy-id "q-337204" :question/problem "A stack of cards has $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack, what is its expected value?\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{4,10\\}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $2$ cards labeled with four and $6$ cards labeled with ten (eight cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4) & =\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =4\\cdot f(4)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4})+10(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90d0c882-c94b-5759-9a78-63979365e318" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Profit of a Game"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f39199e8-353c-5632-85b5-146e5d346bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569826} :answer-field/id #uuid "4197adf1-104f-52af-a2fe-ce58ae6658aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "267e0e90-b604-5e86-ad43-795951237ad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337346" :question/problem "One way to bet in roulette is to place $\\$2$ on a single number. If the ball lands on that number, the player wins $\\$70.$ If the ball lands on any of the other $37$ slots, the player doesn't win. What is the expected profit, rounded to the nearest dollar, for a player who plays one hundred games on number $8$ in a row?\n\nThe expected profit in dollars is $E(p)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First of all, profit is revenue minus cost, or in our case, winnings minus cost. So, once we have found the expected winnings after one hundred games, we need to subtract $100\\cdot 2=200$ dollars to account for the price of playing.\n\nNow, let's find the expected winnings and summarize them in a table. If $W$ is the winnings (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(w)$ is the probability mass function for $W,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(w)$ | $\\frac{1}{38}$ | $\\frac{37}{38}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $w$ | $70$ | $0$ |\n\nThe expected value of $W$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =70\\cdot f(70)+0\\cdot f(0) \\\\  & =70(\\frac{1}{38})+0(\\frac{37}{38}) \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{38} \\\\  & ≈1.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the expected winnings for a single game. So, the expected winnings for $100$ games on number $8$ is\n\n$$\n100\\cdot \\text{E}[W]=100\\cdot (1.84)=184.\n$$\n\nNow, subtracting the $200$ dollars paid to play, we get that the expected profit (in dollars) is\n\n$$\nE[p]=184-200=-16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ce0594-ae9a-5533-b4e8-9b16a4434e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370948} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2d678f-d252-5400-be5e-828422888057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{70}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370949} {:answer/id #uuid "39a17018-6a1b-5fa0-a4b2-d57693172562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370950} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8d0e30-5870-5882-90fe-bbe6d3d8ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{110}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370951} {:answer/id #uuid "11bce5a2-21ae-5099-bf11-e90bee429d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8d0e30-5870-5882-90fe-bbe6d3d8ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{110}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370951} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d39d50-e814-58b3-b920-cbbb549d00fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b33e7f8-97bd-52b2-9fc5-eb73c2b2d7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42732" :question/problem "A bag contains $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills, and $6$ twenty-dollar bills. If one bill is randomly drawn from a bag, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S={5,10,20}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569570} {:answer/id #uuid "6f459d6c-f88c-58f8-8c67-ce4a713307e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569623} {:answer/id #uuid "78fc98f4-275f-5076-bbb7-8cc595a03416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569644} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1705d9-17cc-5143-b4de-f594d074c4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569717} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e43695-a50c-5db3-a1b5-0d7b31b148a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5762b6c1-c01c-597b-9835-929afcb6f899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569570} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec163e0-26a6-57f4-be06-48ae685c5412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d66ccea1-6118-5ac8-bad9-91d326fbbfdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-5775" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a seven-sided die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a standard six-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{7}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=…=f(7)=\\frac{1}{7}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+…+7\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+2(\\frac{1}{7})+…+7(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}+\\frac{2}{7}+…+\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4+5+6+7}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{7} \\\\  & =4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290464f7-629a-599f-9619-f15eb5786d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569498} {:answer/id #uuid "51e0957a-5bf2-56a2-93c7-c85dbc288c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569563} {:answer/id #uuid "5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569576} {:answer/id #uuid "9d79ce2e-0688-5dfd-92d7-ae8f08fcc6bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569694} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a0885c-49d2-5c12-bd6c-2ba68d197915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b73964e-ee01-5caf-b596-26a1127dfc1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569576} :answer-field/id #uuid "850858f3-9f08-5b6d-b191-4d25dc883811" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "522d89ff-41d6-50ec-8d1b-a4ada325fbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-83981" :question/problem "A stack contains four cards, where each card is labeled $1$, $4$, $6$, or $9.$ If one card is randomly drawn, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the label on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S=\\{1,4,6,9\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(4)=f(6)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+4\\cdot f(4)+6\\cdot f(6)+9\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+6(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{6}{4}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+4+6+9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab16145-6ff1-5809-bb97-adbc45c2e916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351662} {:answer/id #uuid "639ce162-6deb-5cdc-aa12-71b9f5fbe5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352452} {:answer/id #uuid "bd54336d-b9c4-5711-b627-5b941c66a638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353180} {:answer/id #uuid "d0020f69-096b-56d4-a5e8-6e4bfea46ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353367} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9d5f73-8fdc-5a4b-a70a-fdac1c36f988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe9d5f73-8fdc-5a4b-a70a-fdac1c36f988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353802} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e0cc8e-72a3-5b78-8684-26b6a6384b0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e4d143c-c13b-5ae0-a77b-3da97ad8ff9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84020" :question/problem "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $2$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $2$ coins?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{9})+1(\\frac{4}{9})+2(\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce3784e-cee7-5852-894c-71ed7ce007ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569465} {:answer/id #uuid "5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569578} {:answer/id #uuid "6e02a023-2534-54ea-a95d-0e9b379d35c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569619} {:answer/id #uuid "a90215ce-141d-5583-8efd-be89ae2f0bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569713} {:answer/id #uuid "ede15bcc-7345-509e-8ca3-6f297ed035d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c751fdf-2bec-56e1-938d-e60711842729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569578} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd980177-3d4f-5c6d-a6cb-2c5b9aaa3857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "700fffbb-cd63-5378-9077-32b4c2add6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84067" :question/problem "Several children were asked how many siblings they have. The number of siblings of each child was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of siblings of a randomly selected child, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of siblings | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of siblings, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $1+5+3+1=10,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+1(\\frac{1}{2})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+6+3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{10} \\\\  & =1.4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4188061c-4dfe-5f94-b792-4dca2da6c67e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569532} {:answer/id #uuid "45c85e36-fafb-5cd0-bf93-acbfc1d73fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569539} {:answer/id #uuid "68868532-f794-5090-9203-a2b2d0d74f1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569606} {:answer/id #uuid "b59463e4-063b-5b43-ba22-7b25a136607c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569732} {:answer/id #uuid "df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df928123-92fc-5c8f-ae4f-3bf6ff6d7789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569798} :answer-field/id #uuid "040b322c-582e-5726-82e2-05dc9e18e0aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0298a94b-23a5-5b8c-89b1-b11dd1bda638" :question/math-academy-id "q-89150" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a four-sided die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the roll of a four-sided die. Then the support is $S=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\nf(1)=f(2)=f(3)=f(4)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)++3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2caf601c-b68b-5641-9bcb-7727613b6286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355049} {:answer/id #uuid "b09bb1f2-5bf8-596e-9a70-aa6dafe756fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356220} {:answer/id #uuid "c7862014-d396-52a6-aec9-f81ecf2bc212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356408} {:answer/id #uuid "e0768a45-d865-522f-9029-613b3fa804b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356627} {:answer/id #uuid "f65fe058-9b55-5802-9726-5819e6757757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65fe058-9b55-5802-9726-5819e6757757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356810} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d0c6279-c1f7-5afc-9b15-a7d1f211a92a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7272ef45-cd69-5899-b223-f4105223d0d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-89152" :question/problem "A fair spinner has six sides each labeled $-2,$ $-1,$ $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ and $6.$ If spinner is spun, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S={-2,-1,1,3,5,6},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569500} {:answer/id #uuid "7566e7ed-5b8d-55f6-bcd8-3e0711ba276d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569639} {:answer/id #uuid "93cd1bc1-ffd4-50f6-955c-6bee087d74b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569675} {:answer/id #uuid "c5540b63-e212-55cb-b7a9-7c7a2846f551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569755} {:answer/id #uuid "c95ceba2-efcb-54f1-bc4a-d6b2a95fef1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a02737d-84cc-5b65-a38a-d8f95f1427b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569500} :answer-field/id #uuid "618772c4-492e-57e3-9e76-dc9f3ada338c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d599b4ec-9437-5cdd-aa0b-91b4481a6586" :question/math-academy-id "q-89157" :question/problem "Several households were asked the number of children that lived there. The number of children in each was recorded below. If $X$ is the number of children that live at a randomly selected household, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Children | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Households | $6$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of childen, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of households is $3+9+6+6=24,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{3}{24}=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3+3+2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
